SMART HOME HUB – LAB REPORT
1. Title
Smart Home Hub: Multi‑Sensor Environmental Monitoring and Control System
2. Objective
The objective of this lab was to design and build a smart‑home controller using an Arduino Uno. The system integrates multiple sensors and actuators to automatically monitor environmental conditions and control devices such as a fan, LED light, and buzzer. The project also includes a user interface via an LCD display and manual override buttons.
3. Components Used
Arduino Uno
16×2 LCD Display
DHT11 Temperature and Humidity Sensor
Photoresistor (LDR) with 10kΩ resistor
L293D Motor Driver
DC Motor (Fan)
LED with 220Ω resistor
Buzzer
Two push buttons
Potentiometer (for LCD contrast)
Breadboard and jumper wires
4. System Overview
The Smart Home Hub continuously monitors temperature, humidity, and ambient light. Based on these readings, it automatically controls a fan, LED light, and buzzer. The LCD displays real‑time sensor data and system status. Two buttons allow manual override of the fan.
